From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: geramyloveless <gloveless@jqluv.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 19:24:16 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [HAL/AMDGPU] macOS coarse host adapter

Builds the AMDGPU HAL over the mac_linuxgpu HSA runtime when compiled
with IREE_HAL_AMDGPU_MACOS_COARSE_HOST_ADAPTER:

- loads libhsa-runtime64.dylib and accepts a runtime without SVM or the
  virtual memory API; without the latter the allocator offers no
  virtual memory;
- pins the system-event callback's image with dladdr and dlopen
  (RTLD_NOLOAD | RTLD_NODELETE) on Darwin, as on Linux, except when HSA
  is linked statically into the same image;
- allows one GPU, host AQL queues and uninstrumented dispatch, clamps the
  AQL ring to the runtime's queue size, forces AQL command buffers and
  host-deferred wait barriers, and disables vendor packets;
- filters CPU agents out of access grants for device-only VRAM, which has
  no CPU mapping on this transport;
- backs hrx_buffer_allocate with one stream-ordered TLSF pool per device
  over the device's shared memory-pool backing, instead of an exact pool
  and a driver allocation per buffer;
- latches CP dispatch profiling at queue creation when HRX_PROFILE_FILE
  and HRX_PROFILE_MODE=dispatch ask for it, and flushes profile events at
  stream synchronization;
- emits a same-queue prefix BARRIER_AND instead of a host round trip when
  every earlier host action on the queue has drained.

Independent of the adapter: the kernel descriptor preserves f32
denormals like the assembly envelope, the system info records whether
the virtual memory API is supported, and a format specifier in
grid_sync.c matches iree_device_size_t on Darwin.
